  "articleBody": "Deciding when to call in a professional for garage wall framing can save you a lot of time, money, and headaches in the long run. Here's when it's definitely time to pick up the phone:\n\n*   **It's a load-bearing wall:** If the wall will support a roof, a second story, or anything significant, you need an expert to ensure it's structurally sound and meets all codes.\n*   **You're dealing with a garage door opening:** Framing for garage doors is trickier than it looks; getting the headers and supports right is crucial for safety and functionality.\n*   **It connects to your main house:** If your garage is attached, there are often specific code requirements, especially around fire separation, that a professional will know how to handle.\n*   **Structural uncertainty or complex design:** If you're unsure about the integrity of an existing structure or have an unusual design in mind, a pro can navigate the complexities.\n*   **Local code questions:** Building codes for stud spacing, lumber size, and anchoring can vary by area. A licensed framer, like the team at HH Remodeling LLC, is up-to-date on all the local regulations in the greater Denver area, from Aurora to Colorado Springs, ensuring your project is compliant and safe. Don't risk costly mistakes or safety hazards when an expert can ensure the job is done right.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
